cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Primordials in academic or pedagogical work, please cite it as below."
title: "Primordials: Real-Time Artificial Life Simulation for the Desktop"
abstract: >
  A real-time artificial life simulation running on the desktop, built on a custom
  C++23 Entity-Component-System engine and a modern React/TypeScript web application.
  Implements continuous Lotka-Volterra predator-prey dynamics with deterministic
  lockstep networking, supporting up to 250,000 entities at 60 frames per second.
  Open source under the MIT license.
type: software
